      "sourceNote": "USDA carries no record for century egg, a duck or hen egg cured for weeks in an alkaline clay-and-ash paste. This is its record for raw whole hen egg, the closest whole-egg profile it publishes; the curing process changes texture and flavour rather than the underlying protein and fat content.",
